+
+/**
+ * METALSHARP_TRACE=<category>[+heavy][,...] turns on the diagnostics a problem needs, in VKD3D-Proton and here:
+ *   shader   per-pipeline Metal compile times, binary archive hits, shader dumps (MVK_CONFIG_SHADER_DUMP_DIR)
+ *   present  one line per present: frame, drawable wait, commit, and when it reached the display
+ *   memory   every VkDeviceMemory and MTLHeap allocation and free, and every texture (MVK_DEBUG_TEXTURES)
+ *   resource (in VKD3D-Proton)
+ *   sync     semaphore, timeline and fence signals and waits, host waits with their duration
+ *   gpu      command buffer errors and a watchdog for command buffers that never complete;
+ *            +heavy adds Metal encoder execution status (MVK_CONFIG_DEBUG)
+ *   cpu      performance statistics every 600 frames (MVK_CONFIG_PERFORMANCE_TRACKING)
+ *   api      Vulkan call trace with durations (MVK_CONFIG_TRACE_VULKAN_CALLS); +heavy adds thread IDs
+ *   pass     every render pass and present (MVK_DEBUG_PASSES)
+ *   all      every category; all+heavy adds every heavy mode
+ * Lines go to <dir>/moltenvk.log (the previous launch's kept as moltenvk.prev.log), where <dir> is
+ * METALSHARP_TRACE_DIR, or <METALSHARP_HOME or ~/.metalsharp>/logs/trace/<exe>, the same folder as VKD3D-Proton's
+ * vkd3d.log. MoltenVK's own log messages go there too while tracing. An MVK_CONFIG_* setting already in the
+ * environment is never overridden.
+ */
